}
```

Then in tests, I can call `parseArgs()` directly with different arguments. This is cleaner and avoids all the ESM module reloading issues.

Let me refactor the CLI module to extract `parseArgs` as a pure function, then also split `main` into testable pieces.

This also makes coverage easier since I can test the logic without spawning real child processes.

